Z||000003||GTDude||12-26-2001||09:36 PM||||Sounds like a bad pressure plate to me, unless it;s a bad master/slave cyl assm.  <BR>Sorry.<BR><P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jncomutt||12-26-2001||09:40 PM||||I would still guess its the hyd. system.  I had a bad slave cyl (frozen) when I first picked up my car.  I got a rebuilt one from Advance Auto Parts and it still didn't work.  I exchanged it for a dif. one and everything works fine.  It may be that you got a bad rebuild...||||reg||1
Z||000005||Rodrv6||12-26-2001||09:57 PM||||I had a similar problem on my 88 GT earlier this summer.  After replacing the master and slave cylinder and bleeding them until I was blue in the face, I still had a clutch that felt soft and wouldn't disengage!!!  I was SURE that the slave cylinder had enough travel, so out came the engine and tranny.  Sure enough, the clutch disc had disintegrated and was the culprit.  A new clutch and everything is fine.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||13
Z||000006||85 gt fiero||12-26-2001||10:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jncomutt:<BR><B>I would still guess its the hyd. system.  I had a bad slave cyl (frozen) when I first picked up my car.  I got a rebuilt one from Advance Auto Parts and it still didn't work.  I exchanged it for a dif. one and everything works fine.  It may be that you got a bad rebuild...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>i would try this method if it doesnt work it doesnt cost anymore <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||LZeitgeist||12-27-2001||06:53 AM||||He had said (if I recall correctly) in another thread (good idea to just continue the previous thread instead of making a new one all over again) that he had about an inch of travel on the slave cylinder rod, and that he'd used Archie's bleeding technique... hopefully he's read about my bleeding screw fiasco and applied that knowledge as well. If all that is true, I'm not sure what else it could be that's outside the tranny itself...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||tesmith66||12-27-2001||07:51 AM||||Is it a four speed?? If so, check the slave cylinder bracket for cracks. It may have to be replaced. Also, if the clutch release arm is stamped steel, toss it and get a cast iron replacement. The stamped ones will crack and flex and cause the problem you are having.<P>Good luck!<P>------------------<BR>Timothy E. Smith<BR>1986 SE V6<BR>1984 Coupe||||reg||1
