Z||000010||LZeitgeist||12-29-2001||12:50 PM||||When the pedal is being depressed, it's pushing air and fluid out. When the bleed screw is closed and the pedal is released, air is being allowed to get sucked back into the system <B>somewhere</B>. <P>If you've never completely removed the bleed screw before, take it out completely and see if there is caked-on gunk preventing it from closing completely. <P>Read through my recent account of a similar problem to see if there's anything in there that will help.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/016622.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/016622.html</A> <P>EDIT - fixed link<p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 12-29-2001).]||||reg||1
